    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1be92359f531a119bfa6fba337bb1cac7b8efb55aaef1445379a6ab6cee8434e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source constructs the fourth-moment formula through a staged change of representation: a four-variable regularization splits a diagonal Ramanujan term from an off-diagonal divisor convolution; additive characters, Mellin inversion, and a functional equation convert the latter into signed Kloosterman kernels; trace formulas then separate those kernels into automorphic spectral channels; only the continued aggregate is specialized back to the target moment.",
