    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_23d3db5b2f4ec2c993f5b8b8a523a31520e83ee3110915ffe56d8f357e5144cc",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Under the stated Gaussian smoothing and parameter range, decay estimates filter the full spectral formula before asymptotic expansion: remote, small, positive, and holomorphic regimes are controlled, the remaining negative real spectral window admits a two-stage saddle-point analysis, and spectral mean bounds then leave the discrete Maass contribution as the leading oscillatory term while the continuous and holomorphic channels are negligible.",
