    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a9002612bba1e04b8af6fe77bee514aa24fc0975165bdf26e2ddcec757bda5a4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The spectral expansion is initially valid only where its rearrangements converge. The source first continues the common five-variable kernel by explicit residue extraction with an arbitrarily deep regular remainder, then continues the continuous spectrum by contour shifting and pole accounting; this makes the off-diagonal term globally meromorphic, permits specialization of the assembled identity at the fourth-moment point, and finally uses aggregate regularity to force cancellation of the singular Laurent parts of the elementary contribution.",
